Title:  Work, Soul and Life

Seq:    12.6.31.1.1

Level:  6 - Subdetail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Camus, Albert|Albert Camus]], 1968, from the book *[[Lyrical and Critical Essays]]*

Timestamp: 20251215020406

Date Added: 2025-12-14 19:04:06 -0700

Date Modified: 2026-10-15 12:27:07 -0600

Referenced In: We make things for one another

Body:

Without work, all life goes rotten. But when work is soulless, life stifles and dies.

